# Act 1, chapter 3 "The Boy Called Goku" (flags 315 opening seen, 316 blueprints taken, 317 self-destruct set,
# 318 chapter over, 319 escape-map arrival seen). Goku never appears on screen: he is "the boy" tearing the base apart.
list ch3_start
set_flag 315
do call 183 516 1454 1455
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1; call 165 0 20
do call 120 1; call 119 1 69 1 216 272; call 121 60
narrate Red Ribbon Army Headquarters. The same night.
narrate Alarms howl through the lower levels. Far above, the command tower is coming apart.
narrate Lab technician: Doctor! The boy is inside the base! The soldiers are throwing down their guns and looting everything they can carry!
say young_gero.1 Let them run. The army is finished... but my work is not.
say young_gero.0 The android blueprints are in the tank room's core. I will not leave them for that boy.
journal Recover the android blueprints from the {c07}tank room{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch3_tech_talk
narrate Lab technician: The terminal still links to your drone, Doctor. The looters won't stand up to it!
list ch3_pod
unless_flag 315 pod_idle
if_flag 316 pod_done
do call 149 0
narrate Gero pulls the memory core from the pod. Years of android research, in the palm of one hand.
say young_gero.3 Everything else can burn. But not before I've wiped the army's archive.
say young_gero.0 Every design I ever gave Commander Red is copied in that vault. I won't leave a single page for that boy... or for anyone.
narrate Lab technician (radio): The archive is past the munitions lines, Doctor. South corridor. The looters got there first.
set_flag 316
journal Wipe the army's archive: south corridor, through the {c07}munitions lines{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label pod_idle
narrate The pod's memory core hums quietly.
stop
label pod_done
narrate The pod is empty. The core is safe in Gero's coat.
list ch3_corridor
narrate The south corridor. The blueprint core comes first.
# ---------- the munitions lines and the archive (areas from log4/gen_ch3.py; flags 283-288)
list ch3_factory
set_flag 283
narrate The munitions lines. Half-built tanks hang from the cranes, and the alarms won't stop.
narrate Looters are stripping the belts for anything they can carry. Their captain has the archive vault's keycard.
say young_gero.1 Thieves. The army isn't even dead yet and they're already picking its bones.
journal Take the vault keycard from the {c07}looters' captain{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch3_vault
set_flag 287
narrate The archive vault. A keycard slot glows beside the blast door.
list vault_locked
narrate The blast door won't move. KEYCARD REQUIRED.
list cache_line
if_flag 288 line_empty
set_flag 288
narrate A crate of field rations at the end of the line. Inside: a tea and two cartons of milk.
do call 129 1 1; call 129 0 2
stop
label line_empty
narrate The crate is empty.
list cache_belt
if_flag 286 belt_empty
set_flag 286
narrate A parts bin under the press. Someone hid a Senzu Bean in it, wrapped in an oily rag.
do call 129 11 1
stop
label belt_empty
narrate Nothing but bolts.
list ch3_archive
if_flag 285 arch_done
set_flag 285
do call 149 0
narrate The archive console. Thousands of files: tanks, airships, drones... and Gero's androids.
say young_gero.0 Delete. All of it.
narrate The progress bar crawls across the screen. Somewhere above, the command tower groans.
say young_gero.2 Twenty years of work for this army. Gone in a minute.
narrate Then he keys in the self-destruct sequence. Ten minutes.
set_flag 317
narrate Archive console: EMERGENCY HATCH OPEN. EXIT TO THE NORTHERN WASTELANDS.
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 71 1 232 440; call 121 30
stop
label arch_done
narrate The screen is blank. There is nothing left to find.
list ch3_escape
set_flag 319
narrate Behind him, the first explosions shake the mountain.
journal Get clear of the base
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch3_end
set_flag 318
do call 149 0
narrate At the old bridge, Gero looks back. The Red Ribbon Army's headquarters burned until morning.
say young_gero.2 Gevo... my army... all of it, gone. Because of one boy.
say young_gero.1 Goku. I will build a soldier that never tires, never doubts and never disobeys. And it will be your end.
do call 120 60
do call 120 1; call 119 1 72 1 112 200; call 121 60
narrate Deep in the northern mountains, Gero found an abandoned Red Ribbon bunker. He would not leave it for years.
journal Rebuild.
do call 47; call 51 0
